{title: 372 - How Beauteous Are Their Feet}
{subtitle: SDA Hymnal #372 • }
{lyricist: }
{composer: }
{key: F}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{meta: hymn_number 372}
{meta: category Christian Church - }

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[F]How beauteous are their [C]feet Who [F]stand on [Bb]Zi[F]on's [C]hill;
[C]Who [F]bring sal[C]vation [F]on [Dm]their [C]tongues, [F]And [Bb]words [F]of peace [C7]re[F]veal!
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[F][C]How [F]charming [Bb]is [F]their [C]voice,
[C][F][C]So [F][Dm]sweet [C][F]the [Bb][F]tidings [C7][F]are:
[F][C]"Zion, [F]behold [Bb]thy [F]Savior [C]King;
[C][F][C]He [F][Dm]reigns [C][F]and [Bb][F]triumphs [C7][F]here!"
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[F][C]How [F]happy [Bb]are [F]our [C]ears,
[C][F][C]That [F][Dm]hear [C][F]the [Bb][F]joyful [C7][F]sound
[F]Which [C]kings [F]and [Bb]prophets [F]waited [C]for,
[C][F][C]And [F][Dm]sought, [C][F]but [Bb][F]never [C7][F]found!
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[F][C]How [F]blessed [Bb]are [F]our [C]eyes,
[C][F][C]That [F][Dm]see [C][F]this [Bb][F]heavenly [C7][F]light;
[F]Prophets [C]and [F]kings [Bb]desired [F]it [C]long,
[C][F][C]But [F][Dm]died [C][F]without [Bb][F]the [C7][F]sight!
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 5}
[F][C]The [F]watchmen [Bb]join [F]their [C]voice,
[C][F][C]And [F][Dm][C]tuneful [F][Bb][F]notes [C7][F]employ;
[F][C]Jerusalem [F]breaks [Bb]forth [F]in [C]songs,
[C][F][C]And [F][Dm]deserts [C][F]learn [Bb][F]the [C7][F]joy.
{end_of_verse}
